1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,000
== Official || kisskh.asia - kissasia.co ||for Support ==

2
00:00:00,143 --> 00:00:01,143
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:01,143 --> 00:00:02,143
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:02,143 --> 00:00:03,176
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:03,176 --> 00:00:06,176
[Episode 3]

6
00:00:07,783 --> 00:00:08,969
- Hello, sir.
- Yeah.

7
00:00:20,339 --> 00:00:22,291
You're going to stare a hole through it.

8
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:24,307
I won't test you, so take it easy.

9
00:00:24,307 --> 00:00:26,900
It's going to be a long haul,
so brace yourself.

10
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,507
Sir, this...

11
00:00:28,507 --> 00:00:30,759
What, what is it?

12
00:00:33,151 --> 00:00:34,726
[Incident Report]
Oh, that case.

13
00:00:34,726 --> 00:00:35,927
The case where a dad was murdered
on Christmas night,

14
00:00:35,927 --> 00:00:37,392
right in front of his daughter.

15
00:00:37,392 --> 00:00:39,092
"He abused his wife and child,

16
00:00:39,092 --> 00:00:41,527
and eventually stabbed his wife
to death with a soju bottle."

17
00:00:41,527 --> 00:00:45,864
"Then, seven years after his release,
he tried to kill his daughter?"

18
00:00:45,864 --> 00:00:48,128
The part about the daughter
was never made public.

19
00:00:48,128 --> 00:00:50,723
She was still a minor at the time,

20
00:00:50,723 --> 00:00:54,383
and she may have been a witness.

21
00:00:54,383 --> 00:00:55,526
A witness?

22
00:00:55,526 --> 00:00:57,127
She saw Kingfisher?

23
00:00:57,127 --> 00:01:01,359
If she had, do you think
we'd still have zero leads?

24
00:01:02,959 --> 00:01:04,707
Well, you never know.

25
00:01:04,707 --> 00:01:08,833
Maybe she really didn't see anything,
or maybe she's keeping quiet.

26
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:12,759
Oh, the daughter's name was 'Oh' something.

27
00:01:24,138 --> 00:01:25,559
Are you crazy?

28
00:01:25,559 --> 00:01:27,359
What are you...

29
00:01:28,011 --> 00:01:30,843
So you really don't want me to die, do you?

30
00:01:30,843 --> 00:01:35,426
The only witness to
one of Kingfisher's shootings.

31
00:01:35,426 --> 00:01:38,592
The only child I ever revealed myself to.

32
00:01:40,579 --> 00:01:43,126
It's been a while, Oh Seung Ah.

33
00:01:57,575 --> 00:02:00,311
Merry Christmas, Yoo Bo Na!

34
00:02:00,311 --> 00:02:01,435
Where's my present?

35
00:02:01,435 --> 00:02:04,607
Santa Claus will bring you one.

36
00:02:04,607 --> 00:02:05,967
Yeah, right. Like he'd ever do that.

37
00:02:05,967 --> 00:02:06,967
You never know.

38
00:02:06,967 --> 00:02:09,411
He's said to have a very clear
sense of right and wrong.

39
00:02:09,411 --> 00:02:11,063
I don't think he's got
a present for you either.

40
00:02:11,063 --> 00:02:13,251
You're a terrible boss for making me
work on a day like this.

41
00:02:13,251 --> 00:02:15,126
It's not like you've got plans.

42
00:02:15,126 --> 00:02:17,767
Do you have friends? A partner? Family?

43
00:02:17,767 --> 00:02:20,295
Yet here you are, all by yourself.

44
00:02:20,295 --> 00:02:23,903
But it's all romance comics, huh?

45
00:02:23,903 --> 00:02:25,191
Seeing someone these days?

46
00:02:25,191 --> 00:02:27,795
Go home early. Kids are waiting.

47
00:02:27,795 --> 00:02:30,007
Will a punk who's meant to die not die
just because you delay it a few days?

48
00:02:30,007 --> 00:02:34,192
He might kill someone first.

49
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:42,326
But isn't it possible he's changed?

50
00:02:42,326 --> 00:02:43,726
Still, he's her dad.

51
00:02:43,726 --> 00:02:48,726
I know, questioning one more time
and never giving up hope until the end.

52
00:02:48,726 --> 00:02:50,967
That's how you do things.

53
00:02:50,967 --> 00:02:53,391
If you want to watch a little longer, do it.

54
00:02:53,391 --> 00:02:57,359
Just don't miss your chance.

55
00:02:58,683 --> 00:03:02,067
It's cold. Take some hand warmers.

56
00:03:02,067 --> 00:03:04,226
I'm off.

57
00:03:07,885 --> 00:03:10,117
[Oh Seung Ah's Daily Route]

58
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:33,587
I thought, "That day
would be the last day of my life."

59
00:03:33,587 --> 00:03:38,092
"It would be my last Christmas."

60
00:03:39,607 --> 00:03:42,492
I thought I'd never see this again.

61
00:03:43,227 --> 00:03:47,391
Whether I died or killed him.

62
00:03:48,879 --> 00:03:52,495
Right, that's probably why.

63
00:03:52,495 --> 00:03:54,459
I heard your heart.

64
00:04:02,355 --> 00:04:04,992
Do you want a Christmas present?

65
00:04:08,395 --> 00:04:10,842
Then no crying.

66
00:04:10,842 --> 00:04:13,026
You have to be good.

67
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:17,859
I heard that Santa is very clear
about right and wrong.

68
00:04:17,859 --> 00:04:19,415
Miss, who are you?

69
00:04:19,415 --> 00:04:23,792
Leave the living room window
slightly open when you get home.

70
00:04:30,007 --> 00:04:31,726
See you again.

71
00:04:34,355 --> 00:04:37,463
Assistant Manager Yoo Bo Na,
what on earth are you doing?

72
00:04:37,463 --> 00:04:40,259
Why would you reveal your face like that?

73
00:04:48,127 --> 00:04:50,326
Does she think she's Santa or something?

74
00:04:50,971 --> 00:04:54,059
She doesn't even know what I wished for.

75
00:05:11,663 --> 00:05:14,546
I prayed to just let me die quickly instead.

76
00:05:14,546 --> 00:05:19,026
If God existed, I begged Him
to save me from hell.

77
00:05:19,026 --> 00:05:21,092
Right at that moment...

78
00:05:30,323 --> 00:05:32,892
God really appeared.

79
00:05:46,391 --> 00:05:48,326
The reason I came back.

80
00:05:49,459 --> 00:05:52,792
The reason I do this.

81
00:05:54,003 --> 00:05:56,759
Hoping to save even just one person.

82
00:05:57,543 --> 00:06:02,026
Hoping that because of this work,
someone might be safe.

83
00:06:04,555 --> 00:06:06,326
You knew all along.

84
00:06:07,743 --> 00:06:10,592
You knew everything
from the start, but why...

85
00:06:12,583 --> 00:06:14,392
Because I was disappointed.

86
00:06:15,359 --> 00:06:20,435
I just wanted that child to be happy

87
00:06:20,435 --> 00:06:23,023
and live a normal life like everyone else,

88
00:06:23,023 --> 00:06:24,692
but that wasn't how things turned out.

89
00:06:25,859 --> 00:06:28,626
I didn't like your choice.

90
00:06:30,759 --> 00:06:32,492
I...

91
00:06:34,792 --> 00:06:37,792
I wanted to be like you.

92
00:06:38,692 --> 00:06:42,592
I wanted to stand beside you someday,

93
00:06:42,592 --> 00:06:46,759
so I've been working myself to death
until now with just that one dream.

94
00:06:50,292 --> 00:06:52,335
You shouldn't have.

95
00:06:52,335 --> 00:06:54,771
You should've followed your own path.

96
00:06:54,771 --> 00:06:57,092
A safe, bright one.

97
00:07:03,623 --> 00:07:06,659
You told me we'd meet again.

98
00:07:08,527 --> 00:07:10,251
What?

99
00:07:13,832 --> 00:07:15,307
See you again.

100
00:07:15,307 --> 00:07:18,792
No, I just meant I hoped you'd stay safe...

101
00:07:18,792 --> 00:07:22,515
I don't know about that,
but anyway, take responsibility.

102
00:07:22,515 --> 00:07:23,967
Me?

103
00:07:23,967 --> 00:07:26,192
You're still such a kid, huh?

104
00:07:27,815 --> 00:07:29,592
What are you?

105
00:07:31,735 --> 00:07:34,526
It was the gift I had desperately wished for.

106
00:07:35,311 --> 00:07:37,627
You were my Santa,

107
00:07:37,627 --> 00:07:39,759
the savior of my life.

108
00:07:42,392 --> 00:07:44,619
So take responsibility.

109
00:07:44,619 --> 00:07:48,063
And yet you drugged my husband?

110
00:07:48,063 --> 00:07:50,867
It wasn't poison. Just a sleeping pill.

111
00:07:50,867 --> 00:07:53,192
Would Kingfisher fall for
something like that?

112
00:07:53,192 --> 00:07:56,059
I know it was a sleeping pill, okay?

113
00:07:56,059 --> 00:07:57,959
Then why bring a gun?

114
00:07:57,959 --> 00:07:59,847
The bullets were real too.

115
00:07:59,847 --> 00:08:01,663
You actually fired it!

116
00:08:01,663 --> 00:08:05,792
Because you messed with someone
you never should have.

117
00:08:11,191 --> 00:08:13,492
What an idiot...

118
00:08:27,943 --> 00:08:30,026
You've really been working hard, huh?

119
00:08:31,867 --> 00:08:33,959
So it was from this point on?

120
00:08:39,931 --> 00:08:42,959
You didn't like my choice either?

121
00:08:42,959 --> 00:08:44,359
About six years ago...

122
00:08:44,359 --> 00:08:47,659
[Six Years Ago]

123
00:08:51,307 --> 00:08:52,559
I saw you by chance.

124
00:08:52,559 --> 00:08:54,087
Honey!

125
00:08:54,087 --> 00:08:56,526
I recognized you instantly.

126
00:08:57,199 --> 00:09:00,159
Because I never forgot you
for a single day after that.

127
00:09:07,519 --> 00:09:11,271
It felt like there was a hole in my chest.

128
00:09:11,271 --> 00:09:13,907
The woman who'd been my god and heroine

129
00:09:13,907 --> 00:09:17,399
had become just an ordinary, fragile person.

130
00:09:17,399 --> 00:09:19,526
So you're more like an anti-fan.

131
00:09:21,926 --> 00:09:24,211
So?

132
00:09:24,211 --> 00:09:25,791
I want to bring you back.

133
00:09:25,791 --> 00:09:28,959
Back to the old Kingfisher,
the woman I used to know.

134
00:09:30,259 --> 00:09:31,775
So you're an idiot after all.

135
00:09:31,775 --> 00:09:33,463
I think I told you.

136
00:09:33,463 --> 00:09:36,895
You made your choice, and I respected it.

137
00:09:36,895 --> 00:09:39,843
Even if I didn't like it, it was your life.

138
00:09:39,843 --> 00:09:41,547
I only did what I had to do.

139
00:09:41,547 --> 00:09:44,492
How you live with it afterward is up to you.

140
00:09:44,492 --> 00:09:46,792
But Kingfisher...

141
00:09:47,623 --> 00:09:50,699
You seem to be mistaken about something.

142
00:09:50,699 --> 00:09:53,392
If I were your savior,

143
00:09:53,392 --> 00:09:56,559
the man who saved Kingfisher
was Kwon Tae Seong.

144
00:09:57,615 --> 00:09:59,355
It was him.

145
00:10:01,135 --> 00:10:02,926
That guy...

146
00:10:03,791 --> 00:10:06,707
saved your life?

147
00:10:06,707 --> 00:10:08,626
He saved something even greater.

148
00:10:11,219 --> 00:10:13,592
I received an even greater gift.

149
00:10:34,339 --> 00:10:36,959
It's Yoo Bo Na!

150
00:10:37,787 --> 00:10:40,143
Honey, do you know where we are now?

151
00:10:40,143 --> 00:10:42,326
A cafe...

152
00:10:44,592 --> 00:10:47,621
Never thought I'd get a call telling me
to pick up my husband from a cafe

153
00:10:47,621 --> 00:10:51,395
because it was closing.

154
00:10:51,395 --> 00:10:53,775
What is going on?

155
00:10:53,775 --> 00:10:55,892
Oh, my!

156
00:10:57,099 --> 00:10:59,926
Did I fall asleep? What? Why?

157
00:11:01,735 --> 00:11:04,259
But when did I fall asleep?

158
00:11:08,063 --> 00:11:09,763
It's nighttime already!

159
00:11:13,627 --> 00:11:15,739
Our date...

160
00:11:15,739 --> 00:11:17,235
Well, it's all over for today.

161
00:11:17,235 --> 00:11:19,392
What are you going to do about this?

162
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,483
I'm sorry. I'll...

163
00:11:24,483 --> 00:11:27,992
I'll do the dishes for a month.
I'm really sorry.

164
00:11:29,723 --> 00:11:31,992
You think that'll make up for it?

165
00:11:35,127 --> 00:11:36,599
No?

166
00:11:36,599 --> 00:11:40,155
I'll also take Yul to daycare
every morning for a month.

167
00:11:40,155 --> 00:11:41,987
I'm really sorry.

168
00:11:41,987 --> 00:11:44,003
Okay, I'll accept that.

169
00:11:44,003 --> 00:11:49,791
And you'll read Yul a bedtime story
every night for a month.

170
00:11:49,791 --> 00:11:51,503
Okay, okay. Deal.

171
00:11:51,503 --> 00:11:52,771
- Okay?
- Yeah.

172
00:11:52,771 --> 00:11:54,855
- Good.
- I'm really sorry.

173
00:11:54,855 --> 00:11:56,443
I ruined our precious time together.

174
00:11:56,443 --> 00:11:59,892
Really, I'll really make it up to you.
Double, I'll really make it up double.

175
00:12:02,575 --> 00:12:03,575
What are we going to do about this?

176
00:12:03,575 --> 00:12:05,826
Honey, I'm so embarrassed.
Let's get out of here.

177
00:12:05,826 --> 00:12:08,926
Se Ah keeps calling. Get up, now.

178
00:12:10,163 --> 00:12:11,231
Are you okay?

179
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:13,136
- I'm okay.
- Can you walk?

180
00:12:13,136 --> 00:12:14,836
Yeah.

181
00:12:16,755 --> 00:12:22,059
If what I fed him was really poison,
I'd have died by your hand, right?

182
00:12:22,863 --> 00:12:24,563
Director.

183
00:12:24,563 --> 00:12:28,792
If you get caught calling me like that
at work too, seriously...

184
00:12:29,571 --> 00:12:31,492
you're really going to die, okay?

185
00:12:33,443 --> 00:12:36,015
At work too...

186
00:12:36,015 --> 00:12:39,126
At work too...

187
00:12:41,126 --> 00:12:43,492
See you at work?

188
00:13:06,892 --> 00:13:11,326
Is family really worth risking your life for?

189
00:13:11,326 --> 00:13:14,192
- Heave-ho!
- Wow!

190
00:13:15,027 --> 00:13:16,726
Mom, I'm hungry.

191
00:13:16,726 --> 00:13:18,155
Yul, are you hungry?

192
00:13:18,155 --> 00:13:19,991
It's time for Yul to eat, isn't it?

193
00:13:19,991 --> 00:13:21,883
Since we're already out,
should we eat out before going home?

194
00:13:21,883 --> 00:13:23,839
Honey, your mom's radish kimchi
is perfectly fermented.

195
00:13:23,839 --> 00:13:25,787
It's because I thought you might be tired.

196
00:13:25,787 --> 00:13:26,992
You said that because
you were worried I'd be tired?

197
00:13:26,992 --> 00:13:28,670
Yeah.

198
00:13:28,670 --> 00:13:30,823
Honey, look at the flowers.
Aren't they pretty?

199
00:13:30,823 --> 00:13:32,159
- You're prettier.
- Really?

200
00:13:32,159 --> 00:13:34,503
- Yeah.
- Is Mommy prettier than flowers?

201
00:13:34,503 --> 00:13:36,726
- Yeah!
- Really?

202
00:13:37,551 --> 00:13:39,626
That was the wrong question.

203
00:13:40,427 --> 00:13:42,663
It's not about risking my life.

204
00:13:42,663 --> 00:13:45,692
My family is my life.

205
00:13:54,687 --> 00:13:57,863
So in the end, he saved one person.

206
00:13:57,863 --> 00:14:01,422
That girl would have died
if it weren't for Kingfisher, right?

207
00:14:01,422 --> 00:14:04,492
So, the conclusion is...

208
00:14:05,623 --> 00:14:07,719
Man, that's just incredible!

209
00:14:07,719 --> 00:14:10,792
That's why he has over a million fans!

210
00:14:11,591 --> 00:14:13,715
Hey, aren't you going to snap out of it?

211
00:14:13,715 --> 00:14:15,626
Is that something a detective should say?

212
00:14:16,615 --> 00:14:18,315
I'm sorry, sir!

213
00:14:18,992 --> 00:14:23,592
Hey, all the victims killed
by Kingfisher were criminals.

214
00:14:23,592 --> 00:14:26,859
But does that justify murder?

215
00:14:26,859 --> 00:14:29,551
- No, it doesn't.
- The law is a social contract.

216
00:14:29,551 --> 00:14:30,815
Does he have the right

217
00:14:30,815 --> 00:14:34,241
to break that contract
and personally judge someone?

218
00:14:34,241 --> 00:14:35,392
- No, he doesn't!
- Should we,

219
00:14:35,392 --> 00:14:37,516
as police officers,
catch someone like that or not?

220
00:14:37,516 --> 00:14:39,959
- We should.
- How?

221
00:14:42,367 --> 00:14:44,455
Well?

222
00:14:44,455 --> 00:14:47,426
That's the conclusion. Got it?

223
00:14:50,899 --> 00:14:53,592
Let's get it together! Get it together!

224
00:14:55,079 --> 00:14:56,459
Here.

225
00:14:56,459 --> 00:14:58,315
Thank you.

226
00:14:58,315 --> 00:14:59,659
Dig through the files all the way.

227
00:14:59,659 --> 00:15:01,559
Up to the final case four years ago.

228
00:15:01,559 --> 00:15:05,326
You'll see another side of Kingfisher.

229
00:15:19,951 --> 00:15:23,126
Hey, don't go too deep.

230
00:15:23,126 --> 00:15:24,626
You might run into snakes.

231
00:15:24,626 --> 00:15:28,792
You have to dig deep to find anything.

232
00:15:30,051 --> 00:15:36,826
The good ones are always
the ones that stay hidden.

233
00:15:45,107 --> 00:15:46,927
What? What's that?

234
00:15:46,927 --> 00:15:49,392
- Is that a snake?
- Over there...

235
00:15:49,392 --> 00:15:51,492
Oh, my...

236
00:15:53,726 --> 00:15:55,959
[Not Today]

237
00:15:55,959 --> 00:15:58,592
[Social Affairs Desk]

238
00:15:59,447 --> 00:16:01,659
[Caller ID Restricted:
I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]

239
00:16:02,495 --> 00:16:05,526
Well, did anyone come by while I was asleep?

240
00:16:05,526 --> 00:16:07,951
Someone who came while you were sleeping?

241
00:16:07,951 --> 00:16:09,147
Yeah.

242
00:16:09,147 --> 00:16:12,726
Well, I don't think I saw anyone.

243
00:16:14,581 --> 00:16:16,248
A tip about Kingfisher?

244
00:16:16,248 --> 00:16:17,646
You scared me!

245
00:16:17,646 --> 00:16:19,631
Jeez, stop popping up
from behind me like that.

246
00:16:19,631 --> 00:16:22,512
My colleague Kwon Tae Seong!

247
00:16:22,512 --> 00:16:23,703
Jeez...

248
00:16:23,703 --> 00:16:25,292
So you finally latched onto
the Kingfisher case, huh?

249
00:16:25,292 --> 00:16:26,526
I knew it.

250
00:16:26,526 --> 00:16:29,326
A swallow can't just pass by a mill, right?

251
00:16:31,895 --> 00:16:34,071
It's a sparrow, not a swallow.

252
00:16:34,071 --> 00:16:37,591
I was going to take it and pass it
to the right person if it was worth pursuing.

253
00:16:37,591 --> 00:16:38,726
What is it?

254
00:16:38,726 --> 00:16:40,287
What is it? What is it?

255
00:16:40,287 --> 00:16:42,257
Is it huge? A scoop?

256
00:16:42,257 --> 00:16:44,826
Did that person really not come?

257
00:16:45,643 --> 00:16:48,292
Or did they come but fail to meet?

258
00:16:48,926 --> 00:16:50,859
There's been no contact since then.

259
00:16:50,859 --> 00:16:53,073
Was it just a prank?

260
00:16:53,073 --> 00:16:54,859
What are you talking about?

261
00:16:56,759 --> 00:17:01,359
But why does my colleague
and economics reporter, Go Ji Soon,

262
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:05,692
always slack off instead of doing his job?

263
00:17:07,667 --> 00:17:10,655
You got stood up, huh? You got stood up.

264
00:17:10,655 --> 00:17:14,179
Man, how can you talk about
being stood up by a source

265
00:17:14,179 --> 00:17:16,692
and make it sound like
an editor-in-chief's report?

266
00:17:17,427 --> 00:17:19,381
Get out of here, you punk!

267
00:17:19,381 --> 00:17:20,955
Keep your chin up, okay?

268
00:17:20,955 --> 00:17:22,655
Fighting!

269
00:17:24,719 --> 00:17:27,591
Hello! Good morning!

270
00:17:27,591 --> 00:17:28,639
Hello.

271
00:17:28,639 --> 00:17:30,535
- Good morning.
- She's so cheerful, isn't she?

272
00:17:30,535 --> 00:17:31,767
- Hello!
- Good morning.

273
00:17:31,767 --> 00:17:34,489
She has no idea
what kind of person her senior is,

274
00:17:34,489 --> 00:17:36,692
and she's still that cheerful.

275
00:17:40,299 --> 00:17:44,555
- Hi.
- Good day. Hello.

276
00:17:44,555 --> 00:17:45,587
Mr. Tae Seong!

277
00:17:45,587 --> 00:17:49,409
I didn't know what you liked,
so I brought one of everything.

278
00:17:49,409 --> 00:17:51,618
Have whichever one you feel like.

279
00:17:51,618 --> 00:17:54,159
I'll take this one. Thank you, Ms. Hae Na.

280
00:17:55,151 --> 00:17:58,292
I already have my usual drink, so I'm fine.

281
00:18:01,263 --> 00:18:03,622
That's not good...

282
00:18:03,622 --> 00:18:05,026
I'll enjoy it then, Ms. Hae Na.

283
00:18:05,026 --> 00:18:07,263
Wow, Mr. Kwon is so lucky.

284
00:18:07,263 --> 00:18:08,327
Thank you, Ms. Hae Na.

285
00:18:08,327 --> 00:18:09,327
Ms. Hae Na, thank you.

286
00:18:09,327 --> 00:18:11,692
There's no one like you, Ms. Hae Na.

287
00:18:24,072 --> 00:18:25,772
Ms. Gu Hae Na.

288
00:18:27,038 --> 00:18:28,595
- Yes!
- Here...

289
00:18:28,595 --> 00:18:31,495
I organized some potential stories
we could look into.

290
00:18:31,495 --> 00:18:34,399
Take a look and let me know
if anything interests you.

291
00:18:34,399 --> 00:18:35,743
- Sorry?
- Oh.

292
00:18:35,743 --> 00:18:38,192
We focus more on in-depth reports
than straight news,

293
00:18:38,192 --> 00:18:39,426
so our investigations take longer.

294
00:18:39,426 --> 00:18:42,792
We'll work on the reporting together
and split the articles.

295
00:18:43,426 --> 00:18:45,392
Yes, sir.

296
00:18:46,726 --> 00:18:48,447
[Managing Child Sex Offenders After Release]
A reporter's job is to prove themselves

297
00:18:48,447 --> 00:18:51,915
through their reporting
and articles above all else.

298
00:18:51,915 --> 00:18:53,615
You know that, right?

299
00:19:01,911 --> 00:19:05,751
What is this? What is this
mysterious character who walks the line

300
00:19:05,751 --> 00:19:07,726
between coldness and passion?

301
00:19:09,226 --> 00:19:11,226
[On-site Inspections
of the Serious Accidents Punishment Act]

302
00:19:11,226 --> 00:19:13,259
[Prison Overcrowding and Parole]

303
00:19:13,259 --> 00:19:14,859
[Voice Phishing Investigations:
Challenges and Solutions]

304
00:19:14,859 --> 00:19:17,983
A reporter who used to dig deeply
into a case or a person

305
00:19:17,983 --> 00:19:20,747
suddenly dropped everything.

306
00:19:20,747 --> 00:19:22,727
That leaves only two possibilities.

307
00:19:22,727 --> 00:19:25,926
They were either paid off or threatened.

308
00:19:27,456 --> 00:19:30,897
Who got what?

309
00:19:30,897 --> 00:19:33,492
Oh, if it were me, I'd take the money.

310
00:19:33,492 --> 00:19:37,226
But he's the type neither of those
would work on.

311
00:19:44,095 --> 00:19:46,183
[Kingfisher Investigation Stalls]
But I feel like the spark

312
00:19:46,183 --> 00:19:48,459
[Identity Unknown]
has not gone out yet.

313
00:19:48,459 --> 00:19:50,792
[Durumi Electronics]

314
00:19:54,903 --> 00:19:56,892
Hello!

315
00:19:56,892 --> 00:19:59,092
[Sales Team 3]

316
00:20:00,359 --> 00:20:02,447
[Team Leader Kim Bong Pal]

317
00:20:02,447 --> 00:20:04,859
- Good morning.
- Thank you, morning candy.

318
00:20:04,859 --> 00:20:05,859
Thank you.

319
00:20:05,859 --> 00:20:07,183
Good morning.

320
00:20:07,183 --> 00:20:08,194
Thank you.

321
00:20:08,194 --> 00:20:10,492
- Good morning!
- Hello.

322
00:20:30,459 --> 00:20:32,026
[Client Report]

323
00:20:32,026 --> 00:20:33,026
Gold.

324
00:20:33,026 --> 00:20:35,059
[Gold: Above the Law Through Money and Power]

325
00:20:35,059 --> 00:20:36,059
White.

326
00:20:36,059 --> 00:20:37,556
[White: Offenders Against
Children and Adolescents]

327
00:20:37,556 --> 00:20:39,259
[Black: Murdered Two or More People]
Black.

328
00:20:39,259 --> 00:20:40,992
[Gray: Pre-Meeting Investigation Subjects]
Gray.

329
00:20:41,755 --> 00:20:43,455
Finish!

330
00:20:53,663 --> 00:20:55,231
I knew you would come, Mr. Lee.

331
00:20:55,231 --> 00:20:56,775
Oh, yeah.

332
00:20:56,775 --> 00:20:59,107
So you got picked
because of your track record.

333
00:20:59,727 --> 00:21:01,035
Oh, my.

334
00:21:01,035 --> 00:21:02,199
Thanks for your hard work.

335
00:21:02,199 --> 00:21:04,011
Track record? What track record?

336
00:21:04,011 --> 00:21:05,583
You didn't know?

337
00:21:05,583 --> 00:21:08,763
Five years ago, taking down
the entire Oh Sun Il gang.

338
00:21:08,763 --> 00:21:10,275
That was Mr. Lee's work.

339
00:21:10,275 --> 00:21:11,703
Oh, that huge case back then!

340
00:21:11,703 --> 00:21:13,155
Amazing!

341
00:21:13,155 --> 00:21:15,647
Oh, so that's why the Chief...

342
00:21:15,647 --> 00:21:18,047
Nothing this time either?

343
00:21:18,047 --> 00:21:20,279
No, nothing.

344
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:23,607
They took the lungs, kidneys,
liver, and pancreas.

345
00:21:23,607 --> 00:21:25,492
They took everything.

346
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:29,792
Judging by the rate of decomposition,
it's been about three or four weeks.

347
00:21:29,792 --> 00:21:35,226
Well, it may have been buried in winter
and decomposed as the weather warmed.

348
00:21:36,542 --> 00:21:39,695
It's been quiet for a while.
Thought it was over.

349
00:21:39,695 --> 00:21:41,887
Honestly, even in the middle of
all that chaos,

350
00:21:41,887 --> 00:21:44,439
they still roughly stitched it up
and dumped it.

351
00:21:44,439 --> 00:21:47,359
They're not fooling around.

352
00:21:47,359 --> 00:21:50,803
They seem even more ruthless
than the last ones.

353
00:21:50,803 --> 00:21:54,492
Mr. Lee, you're going to
have a tough time this time.

354
00:21:59,915 --> 00:22:02,239
[National Forensic Service]
Beom, what is the first thing to do?

355
00:22:02,239 --> 00:22:05,792
Since the victim was reported missing
while hiking on Mount Taegong,

356
00:22:05,792 --> 00:22:07,859
I'll check with the station in charge
about the investigation at the time.

357
00:22:07,859 --> 00:22:08,859
Look into it.

358
00:22:08,859 --> 00:22:11,331
Secure the CCTV footage
from the hiking trail back then too.

359
00:22:11,331 --> 00:22:13,855
Okay. I'll request help with
inquiries around Mount Cheongri,

360
00:22:13,855 --> 00:22:15,538
where the body was found.

361
00:22:15,538 --> 00:22:17,426
Hey, Beom.

362
00:22:17,426 --> 00:22:18,626
You look excited?

363
00:22:18,626 --> 00:22:20,107
[Forensic Imaging Room]

364
00:22:20,107 --> 00:22:21,871
There are so many places to dig into.

365
00:22:21,871 --> 00:22:24,692
These guys are real punks.
Makes me want to catch them even more.

366
00:22:25,539 --> 00:22:29,343
Find out if there were any other
missing persons reports around Mount Taegong.

367
00:22:29,343 --> 00:22:31,159
Also search the database

368
00:22:31,159 --> 00:22:33,995
to see if there have been any similar
unidentified bodies recently.

369
00:22:33,995 --> 00:22:36,167
What? Why is that?

370
00:22:36,167 --> 00:22:38,279
Someone who went missing in Gangwon Province

371
00:22:38,279 --> 00:22:40,792
was found buried in Seoul.

372
00:22:40,792 --> 00:22:45,492
They wouldn't go to that much trouble
just to dispose of one person.

373
00:22:49,035 --> 00:22:50,815
Hey, Beom. Go wait in the car first.

374
00:22:50,815 --> 00:22:52,359
I need to stop by somewhere.

375
00:22:52,359 --> 00:22:54,059
Okay.

376
00:22:56,551 --> 00:22:58,251
Come on! Let's do this!

377
00:23:00,831 --> 00:23:03,159
- Did you send it?
- Yeah, of course.

378
00:23:15,919 --> 00:23:17,619
Oh, dear.

379
00:23:19,443 --> 00:23:22,267
Director Yoo Bo Na, good morning.

380
00:23:22,267 --> 00:23:24,460
Yeah, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

381
00:23:24,460 --> 00:23:26,626
- You are here?
- Yeah.

382
00:23:27,851 --> 00:23:29,711
Let's see.

383
00:23:29,711 --> 00:23:33,223
Oh, my, four people were added today.

384
00:23:33,223 --> 00:23:37,092
Black, Gray, and Gold...

385
00:23:39,292 --> 00:23:43,859
We even have a White
for the first time in a while.

386
00:23:50,603 --> 00:23:51,867
Alright.

387
00:23:51,867 --> 00:23:56,571
We have a new client list,
so let's have a productive meeting.

388
00:23:56,571 --> 00:23:57,839
Yes!

389
00:23:57,839 --> 00:23:59,687
Oh, seriously...

390
00:23:59,687 --> 00:24:02,739
Someone go and bring Manager Bong Tae Min.

391
00:24:02,739 --> 00:24:06,847
Wow, this client is a bit much.

392
00:24:06,847 --> 00:24:08,207
They're not going to be easy.

393
00:24:08,207 --> 00:24:10,987
Jeez, this month is going to be rough.

394
00:24:10,987 --> 00:24:12,339
I'll go get him.

395
00:24:12,339 --> 00:24:14,207
I'll...

396
00:24:14,207 --> 00:24:16,392
I'll go.

397
00:24:17,855 --> 00:24:21,892
That room is pretty nasty. Will she be okay?

398
00:24:21,892 --> 00:24:23,727
I should've given her a mask.

399
00:24:23,727 --> 00:24:27,631
She's used to all kinds of chemicals.

400
00:24:27,631 --> 00:24:29,592
She might actually enjoy it.

401
00:24:30,870 --> 00:24:33,626
Three, two...

402
00:24:36,654 --> 00:24:37,863
Darn it.

403
00:24:53,259 --> 00:24:55,615
This was done by a top-level expert.

404
00:24:55,615 --> 00:24:59,063
You could call it genius-level work.

405
00:24:59,063 --> 00:25:00,275
I looked into it.

406
00:25:00,275 --> 00:25:03,459
As expected, there are no guns
that use this kind of ammunition in Korea,

407
00:25:03,459 --> 00:25:06,059
and I couldn't find any overseas either.

408
00:25:06,059 --> 00:25:10,726
Then someone must have custom-made it.

409
00:25:10,726 --> 00:25:12,826
It was like that from the very first case.

410
00:25:12,826 --> 00:25:15,799
I asked because it seemed like
the bullets had changed this time.

411
00:25:15,799 --> 00:25:19,103
Meaning they upgrade
their equipment every few years.

412
00:25:19,103 --> 00:25:21,479
But if there's
a special top-tier technician like that,

413
00:25:21,479 --> 00:25:23,287
there's no way I wouldn't know.

414
00:25:23,287 --> 00:25:26,235
Does Kingfisher make the weapons themselves?

415
00:25:26,235 --> 00:25:28,111
Probably not. Making them personally...

416
00:25:28,111 --> 00:25:30,326
Well, considering what era we live in,

417
00:25:30,326 --> 00:25:33,759
they probably have
one or two capable assistants.

418
00:25:33,759 --> 00:25:37,559
Well, it could be one or two people,
or it could be an entire team.

419
00:25:37,559 --> 00:25:42,192
They could all be top-tier experts
like you said.

420
00:25:48,343 --> 00:25:50,259
And rice noodles?

421
00:25:55,023 --> 00:25:56,671
Don't get in.

422
00:25:56,671 --> 00:25:57,892
Don't get in.

423
00:25:57,892 --> 00:25:58,959
Don't get in.

424
00:25:58,959 --> 00:26:01,431
- Don't get in.
- Please don't get in.

425
00:26:01,431 --> 00:26:02,779
Oh, that sly punk.

426
00:26:02,779 --> 00:26:04,992
It's spacious, so let's get in.

427
00:26:07,163 --> 00:26:08,859
- Excuse me.
- We'll get in.

428
00:26:08,859 --> 00:26:11,526
- We'll get in.
- Thank you.

429
00:26:19,827 --> 00:26:21,195
I see a new face, huh?

430
00:26:21,195 --> 00:26:25,647
Oh, our Team 3 rookie.

431
00:26:25,647 --> 00:26:28,591
Oh, the one who just joined?

432
00:26:28,591 --> 00:26:30,911
Oh, dear, she's got bad luck.

433
00:26:30,911 --> 00:26:33,943
For a salesperson, where you start matters.

434
00:26:33,943 --> 00:26:35,679
Well, but the timing works out.

435
00:26:35,679 --> 00:26:38,392
You know the whole sales team workshop
is scheduled, right?

436
00:26:38,392 --> 00:26:40,499
Mr. Bong, please take care of it.

437
00:26:40,499 --> 00:26:43,315
Yeah, of course.

438
00:26:43,315 --> 00:26:46,455
Well, adding more people doesn't
automatically improve results.

439
00:26:46,455 --> 00:26:49,711
A small elite team
with the right skills is enough.

440
00:26:49,711 --> 00:26:52,763
A sales technique that silently penetrates,
strikes once, and withdraws.

441
00:26:52,763 --> 00:26:55,826
A true one-shot, one-kill move.

442
00:26:58,327 --> 00:27:01,159
Maybe I should set a date
and give them a special lecture sometime.

443
00:27:01,159 --> 00:27:03,692
- Exactly.
- Enjoy lunch.

444
00:27:08,343 --> 00:27:10,159
That punk...

445
00:27:13,723 --> 00:27:15,759
Let's go eat.

446
00:27:17,015 --> 00:27:18,715
Alright.

447
00:27:21,526 --> 00:27:23,199
This is so great, man.

448
00:27:23,199 --> 00:27:24,435
A three-tier cake.

449
00:27:24,435 --> 00:27:26,226
Oh, I'll prepare that.

450
00:27:26,226 --> 00:27:27,531
Oh, as expected.

451
00:27:27,531 --> 00:27:29,226
I'll definitely prepare a three-tier cake.

452
00:27:29,226 --> 00:27:31,896
Hyun Nam, try to understand.

453
00:27:31,896 --> 00:27:36,559
In sales, performance is
your rank and status.

454
00:27:36,559 --> 00:27:41,335
It must be hard navigating work-life, right?

455
00:27:41,335 --> 00:27:43,187
Speaking of which, Team Leader,

456
00:27:43,187 --> 00:27:47,459
since the results are fake anyway,
do we have to rank last every single time?

457
00:27:47,459 --> 00:27:50,795
I mean, not first place,
but maybe third place once in a while...

458
00:27:50,795 --> 00:27:52,903
Come on!

459
00:27:52,903 --> 00:27:56,631
There are so many people working
their feet off to sell even one more fan.

460
00:27:56,631 --> 00:27:59,552
It's right that we stay at the bottom.

461
00:27:59,552 --> 00:28:03,992
We can't hurt the people who work hard
and give it their all every day.

462
00:28:04,959 --> 00:28:08,319
Alright, then next month
we'll go below each team's

463
00:28:08,319 --> 00:28:10,792
lowest numbers again.

464
00:28:14,301 --> 00:28:17,311
But do we really have to go to a workshop?

465
00:28:17,311 --> 00:28:19,292
Isn't that a bit much?

466
00:28:19,292 --> 00:28:20,542
Normally, we wouldn't.

467
00:28:20,542 --> 00:28:24,427
We don't usually go,
but since you just joined,

468
00:28:24,427 --> 00:28:26,855
it feels awkward to skip it this time.

469
00:28:26,855 --> 00:28:28,719
It seems like a good opportunity to bond

470
00:28:28,719 --> 00:28:30,727
and get some fresh air together
after a long time.

471
00:28:30,727 --> 00:28:33,626
Don't you know a workshop
is still part of work?

472
00:28:36,651 --> 00:28:40,026
What could you even talk about
with people who sell fans?

473
00:28:41,043 --> 00:28:44,611
Sounds fun. I've never been to one before.

474
00:28:44,611 --> 00:28:46,727
Wow, I'm excited.

475
00:28:46,727 --> 00:28:48,692
I can't wait to go.

476
00:28:54,191 --> 00:28:57,243
But Director Yoo, are you okay with it?
It's an overnight trip.

477
00:28:57,243 --> 00:28:58,943
Yeah.

478
00:28:59,963 --> 00:29:02,826
Go Blue Team!

479
00:29:02,826 --> 00:29:04,955
Wow, Team Leader,
you actually look pretty good in that.

480
00:29:04,955 --> 00:29:07,251
Really? I did put some effort in
since we're going to a workshop.

481
00:29:07,251 --> 00:29:08,991
Still, dressing alike like this
really makes it feel like

482
00:29:08,991 --> 00:29:11,092
we're going on a trip, right?

483
00:29:12,339 --> 00:29:14,183
Mommy!

484
00:29:14,183 --> 00:29:15,615
Yul!

485
00:29:15,615 --> 00:29:17,459
Wow, are you going to daycare now?

486
00:29:17,459 --> 00:29:18,459
Yeah.

487
00:29:18,459 --> 00:29:22,671
Yul and Daddy are all ready
and heading out now!

488
00:29:22,671 --> 00:29:25,027
Go, go!

489
00:29:25,027 --> 00:29:27,379
But are you really okay handling it alone?

490
00:29:27,379 --> 00:29:30,867
Should I ask Se Ah
to help out tonight, just in case?

491
00:29:30,867 --> 00:29:34,375
It's okay. I will be fine on my own.

492
00:29:34,375 --> 00:29:37,563
Don't worry and have fun.

493
00:29:37,563 --> 00:29:41,535
Okay, thank you. I will.

494
00:29:41,535 --> 00:29:45,526
Sweetie, want to say
"Have a good trip" to Mommy?

495
00:29:46,339 --> 00:29:47,971
When are you coming back?

496
00:29:47,971 --> 00:29:49,420
Yul, that's not what we talked about.

497
00:29:49,420 --> 00:29:53,915
I told you I'm only sleeping away
for one night, remember?

498
00:29:53,915 --> 00:29:55,147
Yeah, Yul!

499
00:29:55,147 --> 00:29:57,659
Can you be good with Daddy while I'm away?

500
00:29:57,659 --> 00:30:00,047
Where are you going?

501
00:30:00,047 --> 00:30:01,819
Well...

502
00:30:01,819 --> 00:30:03,339
Wait a second.

503
00:30:03,339 --> 00:30:05,579
Yul, we have to do what we practiced.

504
00:30:05,579 --> 00:30:08,592
Sweetie, say goodbye to Mommy!

505
00:30:09,259 --> 00:30:12,603
Mommy, have a safe trip.

506
00:30:12,603 --> 00:30:14,227
A vigorous salute!

507
00:30:14,227 --> 00:30:16,059
Hooah!

508
00:30:16,879 --> 00:30:19,239
Hooah! I'll be back.

509
00:30:19,239 --> 00:30:21,326
Bye, Yul.

510
00:30:22,591 --> 00:30:25,859
Oh, no, she must feel terrible.

511
00:30:27,027 --> 00:30:30,826
It's probably the first time
being this far apart from her kid.

512
00:30:36,547 --> 00:30:37,559
Yes!

513
00:30:37,559 --> 00:30:39,759
Freedom, freedom!

514
00:30:39,759 --> 00:30:42,383
Okay, shall we get going?

515
00:30:42,383 --> 00:30:44,083
Let's get in.

516
00:30:48,896 --> 00:30:51,392
[Durumi Electronics Sales Team Workshop]
Alright, let's go. Let's go.

517
00:30:52,216 --> 00:30:53,971
What did you eat yesterday?

518
00:30:53,971 --> 00:30:55,759
Why did you eat ramyeon?

519
00:30:56,659 --> 00:30:57,779
Sausage too?

520
00:30:57,779 --> 00:31:00,426
Director, look here, please.

521
