00:45:40,105 --> 00:45:42,492
- Maybe this one has more?
- Yes, go ahead.

782
00:45:43,095 --> 00:45:44,885
I'll have this one.

783
00:45:44,885 --> 00:45:46,453
- Yeah.
- Go ahead.

784
00:45:46,453 --> 00:45:47,459
Thank you for the drink.

785
00:45:47,459 --> 00:45:49,459
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

786
00:45:49,459 --> 00:45:52,143
- Thank you.
- Try this one.

787
00:45:52,143 --> 00:45:55,399
This is natural honey.

788
00:45:55,399 --> 00:45:57,215
Thank you so much for the honey water.

789
00:45:57,215 --> 00:45:58,447
Oh, yeah.

790
00:45:58,447 --> 00:46:04,026
- Bottoms up!
- Bottoms up!

791
00:46:07,953 --> 00:46:09,653
Thank you.

792
00:46:10,503 --> 00:46:14,159
- It's really sweet.
- Then enjoy yourselves.

793
00:46:14,159 --> 00:46:16,615
- Oh, yeah.
- Yes.

794
00:46:16,615 --> 00:46:18,315
Keep drinking.

795
00:46:19,300 --> 00:46:21,026
Yeah, got it.

796
00:46:35,995 --> 00:46:38,259
These punks are crossing the line.

797
00:46:41,171 --> 00:46:42,583
[Mount Taegong Missing Persons Map]
Their hideout is believed to be

798
00:46:42,583 --> 00:46:47,792
Taegong Grandpa Pension
on the east side of Mount Taegong.

799
00:46:55,699 --> 00:47:00,291
But we still don't have any solid evidence.

800
00:47:00,291 --> 00:47:03,526
You know the whole sales team workshop
is scheduled, right?

801
00:47:03,526 --> 00:47:05,430
Mr. Bong, please take care of it.

802
00:47:05,430 --> 00:47:08,192
Yeah, of course.

803
00:47:11,467 --> 00:47:13,359
Let's go!

804
00:47:16,075 --> 00:47:17,167
Remember,

805
00:47:17,167 --> 00:47:21,071
the goal is gathering information,
not a meeting.

806
00:47:21,071 --> 00:47:24,503
And remember, their safety comes first.

807
00:47:24,503 --> 00:47:26,203
Yes!

808
00:47:43,559 --> 00:47:44,903
The entire exterior of the building

809
00:47:44,903 --> 00:47:46,972
is equipped with electromagnetic
shielding devices.

810
00:47:46,972 --> 00:47:49,992
It seems designed to cut off communication
with the outside in case of an emergency.

811
00:48:38,935 --> 00:48:41,187
- Bingo!
- Excuse me, Ma'am.

812
00:48:41,187 --> 00:48:46,209
Which one did you put the most honey in?

813
00:48:46,209 --> 00:48:47,434
It's not dangerous.

814
00:48:47,434 --> 00:48:48,683
It's just a sleeping pill.

815
00:48:48,683 --> 00:48:51,126
I'll have this one.

816
00:48:52,291 --> 00:48:54,192
It's an antidote.

817
00:48:57,164 --> 00:49:00,551
They've never gone after guests before.

818
00:49:00,551 --> 00:49:02,083
They must have lost their minds.

819
00:49:02,083 --> 00:49:06,483
Now that the police are onto them,
they're trying to make one big score and run.

820
00:49:06,483 --> 00:49:08,347
We'll keep monitoring the situation for now.

821
00:49:08,347 --> 00:49:10,271
By the way, I haven't seen
Tae Min for a while.

822
00:49:10,271 --> 00:49:12,492
Assistant Manager Ki went out
because his communication wasn't working.

823
00:49:12,492 --> 00:49:14,244
The phones are dead too.

824
00:49:14,244 --> 00:49:16,111
They must have activated the device.

825
00:49:16,111 --> 00:49:18,001
Darn it.

826
00:49:18,001 --> 00:49:19,859
I'll go find him.

827
00:49:23,627 --> 00:49:25,819
Please look after Director Yoo.

828
00:49:25,819 --> 00:49:27,592
Got it. So hurry back.

829
00:49:35,867 --> 00:49:38,015
Assistant Manager Ki!

830
00:49:38,015 --> 00:49:40,159
Manager Tae Min!

831
00:49:40,791 --> 00:49:43,059
Where are they?

832
00:49:44,459 --> 00:49:46,547
Assistant Manager Ki!

833
00:49:46,547 --> 00:49:48,759
Manager Tae Min!

834
00:50:06,899 --> 00:50:08,599
Oh, seriously.

835
00:50:16,033 --> 00:50:18,359
What's that in their hands?

836
00:50:23,175 --> 00:50:25,375
Wow, how much is all this?

837
00:50:25,375 --> 00:50:28,500
We hit the jackpot today.

838
00:50:28,500 --> 00:50:30,145
Tie them all up!

839
00:50:30,145 --> 00:50:31,992
Yes!

840
00:50:32,959 --> 00:50:36,887
It's actually better that they passed out
from the sleeping pills.

841
00:50:36,887 --> 00:50:38,759
Jeez, crazy punks.

842
00:50:38,759 --> 00:50:42,326
Forget those lunatics for now.
Let's find Assistant Manager Ki first.

843
00:50:42,326 --> 00:50:45,426
His comms have been dead for a while.
Looks like they got him.

844
00:50:46,792 --> 00:50:48,792
Think he's already dead?

845
00:50:48,792 --> 00:50:50,526
Excuse me.

846
00:50:51,763 --> 00:50:54,167
If he's alive, he has to be
somewhere around here.

847
00:50:54,167 --> 00:50:56,559
No cars have left the property.

848
00:51:04,503 --> 00:51:06,626
Tie them up tight.

849
00:51:06,626 --> 00:51:10,459
Hey, move your head, jeez.

850
00:51:15,473 --> 00:51:16,971
What's with these people?

851
00:51:16,971 --> 00:51:18,283
Why are they still awake?

852
00:51:18,283 --> 00:51:20,015
Hey, folks.

853
00:51:20,015 --> 00:51:24,026
If you keep this up, things are
going to get difficult for you.

854
00:51:26,043 --> 00:51:28,592
Wow, listen to me talking.

855
00:51:29,643 --> 00:51:30,719
Old man!

856
00:51:30,719 --> 00:51:33,811
Some of them are still awake.
What do we do? Kill them?

857
00:51:33,811 --> 00:51:35,626
Are you insane?

858
00:51:38,804 --> 00:51:40,733
They're worth 300 million won each.

859
00:51:40,733 --> 00:51:42,433
300 million won.

860
00:51:45,747 --> 00:51:49,336
That old hag got distracted again.

861
00:51:49,336 --> 00:51:50,895
Just tie them up for now.

862
00:51:50,895 --> 00:51:52,759
Or knock them out.

863
00:51:52,759 --> 00:51:55,383
How exactly do you knock someone out?

864
00:51:55,383 --> 00:51:57,619
I don't want to be hurt.

865
00:51:57,619 --> 00:52:00,259
Darn, my phone's dead again.

866
00:52:00,259 --> 00:52:01,779
That's a problem, isn't it?

867
00:52:01,779 --> 00:52:05,159
What? You're going to call the cops?

868
00:52:05,159 --> 00:52:07,326
- Give me a break.
- Come on.

869
00:52:07,326 --> 00:52:10,559
Friend, don't be like that.
Let's just talk this out...

870
00:52:11,759 --> 00:52:12,826
- Team Leader!
- Team Leader!

871
00:52:12,826 --> 00:52:13,919
We'll communicate physically.

872
00:52:13,919 --> 00:52:17,092
- You punks...
- My fists have been itching anyway.

873
00:52:17,092 --> 00:52:19,026
Don't rush your death.

874
00:52:19,026 --> 00:52:20,292
Hey, just keep your mouth shut.

875
00:52:20,292 --> 00:52:21,359
Knife! Knife! Knife!

876
00:52:21,359 --> 00:52:23,726
Please save me.

877
00:52:23,726 --> 00:52:25,626
Please save me!

878
00:52:26,592 --> 00:52:29,303
- Team Leader!
- There's a girl over there.

879
00:52:29,303 --> 00:52:31,926
Go tie her up.
Tie up everyone over there and here.

880
00:52:34,744 --> 00:52:36,363
You're going to regret this.

881
00:52:36,363 --> 00:52:37,383
We'll regret it?

882
00:52:37,383 --> 00:52:38,383
Team Leader?

883
00:52:38,383 --> 00:52:40,426
Put that down.

884
00:52:46,053 --> 00:52:48,455
Your call cannot be connected
and is being forwarded to voicemail.

885
00:52:48,455 --> 00:52:49,867
After the beep...

886
00:52:52,143 --> 00:52:54,985
What should we do?
Mommy keeps not answering her phone.

887
00:52:54,985 --> 00:52:58,299
I miss mommy.

888
00:52:58,299 --> 00:53:00,036
You miss mommy?

889
00:53:00,036 --> 00:53:03,411
I miss Mommy a lot too.

890
00:53:03,411 --> 00:53:05,563
Why isn't Mommy answering?

891
00:53:05,563 --> 00:53:09,059
Mommy is deep in the woods right now.

892
00:53:09,059 --> 00:53:10,933
So the phone signal isn't good there.

893
00:53:10,933 --> 00:53:12,143
In the woods?

894
00:53:12,143 --> 00:53:17,684
Then what if Mommy meets a wolf
like Little Red Riding Hood?

895
00:53:17,684 --> 00:53:19,384
What?

896
00:53:20,824 --> 00:53:22,492
Is it here?

897
00:53:22,492 --> 00:53:24,826
It's locked. What do we do?

898
00:53:32,686 --> 00:53:34,386
Wow...

899
00:53:55,679 --> 00:53:58,359
Assistant Manager Ki, are you in there?

900
00:53:59,827 --> 00:54:01,527
Hey!

901
00:54:09,071 --> 00:54:11,192
Here, here!

902
00:54:14,392 --> 00:54:17,046
Hurry, hurry.

903
00:54:17,046 --> 00:54:20,659
What a surprise. Our Assistant Manager Ki
has gone missing in action again?

904
00:54:23,959 --> 00:54:26,107
You really never disappoint.

905
00:54:26,107 --> 00:54:29,859
Isn't it proper to be surprised
and worried at a time like this?

906
00:54:29,859 --> 00:54:32,526
Oh, my, what do we do? Are you okay?

907
00:54:33,333 --> 00:54:35,259
Do you two not get along?

908
00:54:36,192 --> 00:54:39,223
Well, how awful.

909
00:54:39,223 --> 00:54:40,223
What's it like in there?

910
00:54:40,223 --> 00:54:42,095
They've already stormed in.

911
00:54:42,095 --> 00:54:43,292
There are quite a few of them.

912
00:54:43,292 --> 00:54:44,501
Looks like they planned this.

913
00:54:44,501 --> 00:54:46,179
Shouldn't we hurry and go?

914
00:54:46,179 --> 00:54:48,026
They've probably already started fighting.

915
00:54:48,026 --> 00:54:49,726
Yeah.

916
00:54:50,623 --> 00:54:52,323
Yeah.

917
00:54:54,074 --> 00:54:57,118
Team Leader!

918
00:54:57,118 --> 00:55:00,059
- I won't let you go, you punks.
- Ouch!

919
00:55:02,739 --> 00:55:04,736
Can't we touch them? Why?

920
00:55:04,736 --> 00:55:06,284
They're gray.

921
00:55:06,284 --> 00:55:09,926
- What?
- They're not approved for a meeting yet.

922
00:55:09,926 --> 00:55:12,049
Gray means they're still under investigation,
not confirmed clients.

923
00:55:12,049 --> 00:55:13,667
Don't you know that?

924
00:55:13,667 --> 00:55:15,779
I know that much.

925
00:55:15,779 --> 00:55:18,126
But they attacked us first!

926
00:55:18,126 --> 00:55:23,526
Under no circumstances
do we conduct a meeting with a non-client.

927
00:55:23,526 --> 00:55:25,608
We only deal with targets

928
00:55:25,608 --> 00:55:28,215
that have been verified multiple times

929
00:55:28,215 --> 00:55:32,059
and finally approved through the system.

930
00:55:32,059 --> 00:55:34,192
That's our rule.

931
00:55:35,483 --> 00:55:36,892
So we're just supposed to
sit here and take it?

932
00:55:36,892 --> 00:55:38,808
There are other people in there too.

933
00:55:38,808 --> 00:55:42,059
Don't worry so much. I said it's not yet.

934
00:55:43,256 --> 00:55:44,992
Tie them up tight.

935
00:55:44,992 --> 00:55:47,359
Hurry up.

936
00:55:47,359 --> 00:55:49,459
Do it properly.

937
00:55:53,603 --> 00:55:55,926
Team Leader, are you okay?

938
00:55:57,356 --> 00:55:59,707
I'm fine.

939
00:55:59,707 --> 00:56:03,391
They wouldn't actually kill us, would they?

940
00:56:03,391 --> 00:56:04,391
We will.

941
00:56:04,391 --> 00:56:06,567
Oh, yeah?

942
00:56:06,567 --> 00:56:07,659
And how are you planning to do that?

943
00:56:07,659 --> 00:56:09,939
How would you like to die?

944
00:56:09,939 --> 00:56:11,859
Should I specially cut your belly open
while you're alive?

945
00:56:11,859 --> 00:56:12,926
Come on.

946
00:56:12,926 --> 00:56:14,723
- Oh.
- No.

947
00:56:14,723 --> 00:56:17,926
Since your eyes are so sparkly,
I should gouge those out first.

948
00:56:17,926 --> 00:56:19,492
They still look like they're worth something.

949
00:56:19,492 --> 00:56:23,243
That's right. I've got the best eyesight.

950
00:56:23,243 --> 00:56:25,007
I've eaten a lot of lettuce.

951
00:56:25,007 --> 00:56:26,959
Beta-carotene, you know.

952
00:56:27,771 --> 00:56:29,579
B-B-Beta what?

953
00:56:29,579 --> 00:56:32,226
Beta-carotene, you moron.

954
00:56:33,192 --> 00:56:35,059
Why are you even entertaining his nonsense?

955
00:56:35,059 --> 00:56:37,351
Stop the nonsense and move them
to the warehouse quickly.

956
00:56:37,351 --> 00:56:41,583
And call Dr. Jo to come in
early in the morning!

957
00:56:41,583 --> 00:56:43,926
Contact all the clients.

958
00:56:45,724 --> 00:56:48,214
They'll love this.

959
00:56:48,214 --> 00:56:51,392
They're all young and healthy.

960
00:56:52,471 --> 00:56:54,723
I think we're really going to die.
What do we do?

961
00:56:54,723 --> 00:56:56,534
Oh, don't worry.

962
00:56:56,534 --> 00:57:00,895
My fortune says I'll live to 150.

963
00:57:00,895 --> 00:57:02,399
You're full of it.

964
00:57:02,399 --> 00:57:05,871
Hey, you punk, what have you been
staring at so intently?

965
00:57:05,871 --> 00:57:08,043
The phone, idiot. That phone.

966
00:57:08,043 --> 00:57:10,959
The phone doesn't even work. Darn it!

967
00:57:13,692 --> 00:57:15,392
What?

968
00:57:16,775 --> 00:57:17,901
Huh? What is it?

969
00:57:23,923 --> 00:57:26,326
[Emergency Notice]
"Pre-meeting with the client approved"?

970
00:57:26,326 --> 00:57:27,326
What is this?

971
00:57:27,326 --> 00:57:29,526
Looks like we finally got approval.

972
00:57:34,759 --> 00:57:38,759
Alright, let's slowly start our meeting.

973
00:57:43,415 --> 00:57:46,359
It's done. We've arrived.

974
00:57:46,359 --> 00:57:48,058
Found it.

975
00:57:48,058 --> 00:57:49,431
I've sent the evidence.

976
00:57:49,431 --> 00:57:51,479
Requesting emergency meeting approval.

977
00:57:51,479 --> 00:57:52,659
So what do we do now?

978
00:57:52,659 --> 00:57:56,324
They're heavily armed.
What if it comes down to hand-to-hand combat?

979
00:57:56,324 --> 00:57:58,159
You're worrying for nothing again.

980
00:58:03,291 --> 00:58:06,387
Team leader served
in the Army Special Forces.

981
00:58:06,387 --> 00:58:09,126
He's especially skilled
in close-quarters combat.

982
00:58:11,007 --> 00:58:13,071
Oh, my.

983
00:58:13,071 --> 00:58:15,507
Assistant Manager Yang's hobby
is every combat sport imaginable.

984
00:58:15,507 --> 00:58:18,559
Judo, taekwondo, kickboxing...

985
00:58:18,559 --> 00:58:20,659
There's nothing she can't do.

986
00:58:26,663 --> 00:58:28,363
Jeez.

987
00:58:31,635 --> 00:58:34,526
You are all bark and no bite.

988
00:58:36,103 --> 00:58:37,999
Director!

989
00:58:37,999 --> 00:58:39,699
Director!

990
00:58:45,435 --> 00:58:48,292
Hands up, you punk!

991
00:58:50,015 --> 00:58:51,715
Oh, dear.

992
00:58:52,949 --> 00:58:55,192
An elderly person like you...

993
00:58:55,841 --> 00:59:00,892
shouldn't be playing
with dangerous things like this.

994
00:59:01,786 --> 00:59:03,822
Oh, that's hot!

995
00:59:03,822 --> 00:59:08,092
Shut up! Face the wall,
and put your hands up.

996
00:59:09,861 --> 00:59:11,626
Hurry!

997
00:59:16,542 --> 00:59:18,242
The rest of you too!

998
00:59:20,819 --> 00:59:23,192
Hey, move them against the wall!

999
00:59:25,707 --> 00:59:26,859
Team Leader!

1000
00:59:26,859 --> 00:59:29,626
Hey, step on him.

1001
00:59:32,659 --> 00:59:35,018
Hey, hey!

1002
00:59:35,018 --> 00:59:37,592
If possible, don't touch the stomach area.

1003
00:59:37,592 --> 00:59:40,826
- It's 300 million won each!
- Yes!

1004
00:59:46,755 --> 00:59:50,907
Then what if a wolf shows up
while Mommy's in the woods?

1005
00:59:50,907 --> 00:59:53,201
The wolf would be too scared and run away.

1006
00:59:53,201 --> 00:59:55,495
Mommy's stronger than the wolf?

1007
00:59:55,495 --> 00:59:59,626
Of course, Mommy is much stronger.
Mommy's super strong.

1008
00:59:59,626 --> 01:00:04,079
She can climb the roughest
mountain trails like it's nothing.

1009
01:00:04,079 --> 01:00:09,089
Even through deep snow,
she plows a path like a bulldozer.

1010
01:00:09,089 --> 01:00:12,827
She's so strong
that she can lift me with ease.

1011
01:00:12,827 --> 01:00:16,792
Well... And...

1012
01:00:18,915 --> 01:00:22,292
She's really fearless...

1013
01:00:26,843 --> 01:00:28,780
The Mommy I know

1014
01:00:28,780 --> 01:00:33,387
is a wonderful person
who is rough and strong,

1015
01:00:33,387 --> 01:00:35,592
yet never loses her grace.

1016
01:00:36,659 --> 01:00:38,463
What is it?

1017
01:00:38,463 --> 01:00:40,926
Why's it so darn noisy?

1018
01:00:42,311 --> 01:00:44,292
Well.

1019
01:00:47,939 --> 01:00:49,915
Director Yoo is awake.

1020
01:00:49,915 --> 01:00:51,235
Director Yoo.

1021
01:00:51,235 --> 01:00:54,083
Oh, darn it, who is it? You noisy punks.

1022
01:00:54,083 --> 01:00:55,999
I can't sleep.

1023
01:00:55,999 --> 01:00:57,595
What's this? Who did this?

1024
01:00:57,595 --> 01:00:59,426
Who tied me up like this?

1025
01:00:59,426 --> 01:01:03,541
- Was it you?
- What's with that woman?

1026
01:01:03,541 --> 01:01:07,226
Where did all these darn flies come from?

1027
01:01:07,226 --> 01:01:08,592
What? Flies?

1028
01:01:08,592 --> 01:01:10,926
Flies? You crazy punk!

1029
01:01:15,859 --> 01:01:18,792
You said you could handle it alone.
Did you get old already? Huh?

1030
01:01:18,792 --> 01:01:21,367
Well, I've been at it for months.

1031
01:01:21,367 --> 01:01:23,759
I figured I'd at least try doing it myself.

1032
01:01:23,759 --> 01:01:26,284
It was your first outing in a while.

1033
01:01:26,284 --> 01:01:30,251
I wanted you to drink, sleep well,
and enjoy yourself.

1034
01:01:30,251 --> 01:01:35,295
Then this old geezer suddenly
showed up with a gun.

1035
01:01:35,295 --> 01:01:36,523
- A gun?
- Yeah.

1036
01:01:36,523 --> 01:01:38,492
He's got a gun?

1037
01:01:39,551 --> 01:01:42,239
Director Yoo, take care of this.

1038
01:01:42,239 --> 01:01:44,959
Move, you punks.

1039
01:01:47,315 --> 01:01:49,250
Hey!

1040
01:01:49,250 --> 01:01:50,943
You, kneel.

1041
01:01:50,943 --> 01:01:52,599
Yeah, kneel.

1042
01:01:52,599 --> 01:01:53,892
Get on your knees, you punk!

1043
01:01:53,892 --> 01:01:56,859
Where'd this old fly come buzzing from?

1044
01:01:57,951 --> 01:01:59,778
That punk...

1045
01:01:59,778 --> 01:02:02,492
You want a hole in your head?

1046
01:02:03,591 --> 01:02:05,250
"A hole in your head"?

1047
01:02:05,250 --> 01:02:06,950
That's my line.

1048
01:02:08,250 --> 01:02:10,003
Oh, jeez, I...

1049
01:02:10,003 --> 01:02:14,354
Don't move! Move, and I'll shoot!

1050
01:02:14,354 --> 01:02:16,459
If I move, you won't be able to hit me.

1051
01:02:17,859 --> 01:02:22,007
Seriously... Has she lost her mind?

1052
01:02:22,007 --> 01:02:24,626
Go ahead. I'm staying still here.

1053
01:02:28,126 --> 01:02:29,907
T-T-That's right.

1054
01:02:29,907 --> 01:02:31,892
Die, you punk!

1055
01:02:33,992 --> 01:02:36,326
Old man!

1056
01:02:36,326 --> 01:02:39,792
- Old man.
- You couldn't even shoot me?

1057
01:02:42,834 --> 01:02:44,659
I won't shoot. I won't.

1058
01:02:44,659 --> 01:02:46,359
You won't shoot?

1059
01:02:53,159 --> 01:02:54,329
Time to go.

1060
01:02:54,329 --> 01:02:56,115
Hey! Kill that punk!

1061
01:02:56,115 --> 01:02:57,695
Shall I go for it after a long time?

1062
01:02:57,695 --> 01:02:59,559
Come at me all at once, you flies!

1063
01:02:59,559 --> 01:03:01,559
Hey! Kill that punk!

1064
01:03:04,592 --> 01:03:06,846
Missed.

1065
01:03:06,846 --> 01:03:08,626
Guess I'll just go then.

1066
01:03:09,592 --> 01:03:11,359
Hey, you punk!

1067
01:03:33,547 --> 01:03:35,859
Yoo Bo Na's drunk habit is out.

1068
01:03:38,211 --> 01:03:39,911
Bo Na...

1069
01:03:50,471 --> 01:03:52,892
Why do you keep getting up?

1070
01:04:06,618 --> 01:04:08,892
A woman as agile as a puma,

1071
01:04:08,892 --> 01:04:11,017
as mighty as a lion,

1072
01:04:11,017 --> 01:04:13,607
and as graceful as a swan.

1073
01:04:13,607 --> 01:04:15,559
Yoo Bo Na looked

1074
01:04:16,415 --> 01:04:18,792
truly beautiful then.

1075
01:04:53,692 --> 01:04:55,592
Get on your knees, you punk!

1076
01:05:02,192 --> 01:05:04,926
Director Yoo's still got it!

1077
01:05:40,705 --> 01:05:43,862
Yul, I told you I have to
go to work today, so I can't, right?

1078
01:05:43,862 --> 01:05:44,867
I hate you, Mommy.

1079
01:05:44,867 --> 01:05:46,783
So this guy is getting out after all?

1080
01:05:46,783 --> 01:05:48,807
But we should move up the timeline.

1081
01:05:48,807 --> 01:05:50,354
Before he returns to his neighborhood.

1082
01:05:50,354 --> 01:05:51,975
That'll cause quite a stir.

1083
01:05:51,975 --> 01:05:54,011
He died the day he was released.

1084
01:05:54,011 --> 01:05:56,392
What if we followed the crimes
before they happen?

1085
01:05:56,392 --> 01:05:58,607
Sir, welcome.

1086
01:05:58,607 --> 01:06:00,195
Kingfisher's next target.

1087
01:06:00,195 --> 01:06:01,626
Is this connected to Kingfisher?

1088
01:06:01,626 --> 01:06:03,859
Were you following me?

1089
01:06:03,859 --> 01:06:05,211
What's going on? Team Leader!

1090
01:06:05,211 --> 01:06:07,992
I'm Pyo Kyu Cheol, you punks!

1091
01:06:07,992 --> 01:06:11,003
That puts Director Yoo
in the most dangerous position.

1092
01:06:11,003 --> 01:06:13,559
She's also the most likely to get caught.
